1
00:00:00,492 --> 00:00:02,496
[Bus plunged from bridge; 12 dead, 1 missing]
Did you see the news?

2
00:00:02,496 --> 00:00:04,880
A bus plunged off a bridge
not too far from here.

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:09,280
And it appears my husband was on board.
They haven't found him yet.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:15,106
My wife was on that same bus,
and she was dead.

5
00:00:17,301 --> 00:00:21,655
Your husband was
having an affair with my wife.

6
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:26,368
It's the 'loved one filter,' right?

7
00:00:27,603 --> 00:00:29,454
You should clean it.

8
00:00:31,774 --> 00:00:35,961
Are you listening?
Your husband and my wife...

9
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,867
No, no, no.

10
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:44,511
It's fine, it's fine. That sort of thing.

11
00:00:50,668 --> 00:00:54,896
You really do come up with
such interesting ideas, Mr. Sonoda.

12
00:00:55,839 --> 00:00:58,496
Do you like movies or novels?

13
00:00:58,496 --> 00:00:59,940
The third Friday.

14
00:01:01,856 --> 00:01:04,781
Doesn't your husband take
the third Friday off every month?

15
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:08,700
Yes, he runs a coffee shop.

16
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:11,719
- His regular day off is Friday...
- Friday, right?

17
00:01:12,523 --> 00:01:15,872
Well... What is it?

18
00:01:16,777 --> 00:01:22,272
Is that, well... something that
people who have Fridays off do?

19
00:01:22,272 --> 00:01:25,184
Have an affair, right? Have an affair.

20
00:01:25,184 --> 00:01:27,037
Seriously, can you stop that?

21
00:01:27,037 --> 00:01:28,622
Stop what?

22
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,224
Making false accusations. Please stop it.

23
00:01:31,834 --> 00:01:33,877
There's absolutely no way
my husband would do that.

24
00:01:33,877 --> 00:01:36,104
You're lucky that you can think like that.

25
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,555
- Well...
- Yes?

26
00:01:44,555 --> 00:01:46,890
What about the third Friday of every month?

27
00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:49,643
Since you've already said that much,
I'd like you to explain it all the way.

28
00:01:49,643 --> 00:01:52,479
And after I hear your theory,
I want to properly refute it.

29
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,824
There's absolutely no way he did that.

30
00:01:53,824 --> 00:01:56,320
No. If I tell you the facts,
will you just deny them?

31
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:59,232
- Come on, that's unpleasant.
- You're being unpleasant today, Mr. Sonoda.

32
00:01:59,232 --> 00:02:01,080
This is how I normally am.

33
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,720
No, it's you who can't show your true nature.

34
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,224
You're the wife of the person

35
00:02:04,224 --> 00:02:05,884
- my wife had an affair with.
- That's why.

36
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,608
Hold on.

37
00:02:08,608 --> 00:02:11,973
No, no, it's just that we've talked a lot,
and I'm getting a little thirsty.

38
00:02:28,807 --> 00:02:31,326
I accidentally bought two.

39
00:02:43,489 --> 00:02:48,301
Let me explain quickly
while the laundry dries.

40
00:02:52,372 --> 00:02:58,045
That day was the third Friday of May.

41
00:02:58,045 --> 00:03:00,355
[Friday, May 16]

42
00:03:01,465 --> 00:03:05,504
<i>I realized that I'd left the materials
I needed for an afternoon meeting at home,</i>

43
00:03:05,504 --> 00:03:08,238
<i>so I thought I'd ask my wife
to bring them to me.</i>

44
00:03:09,098 --> 00:03:13,435
<i>She worked part-time at a used bookstore,
but she was off that day.</i>

45
00:03:13,435 --> 00:03:17,248
<i>But I felt bad bothering her on her day off.</i>

46
00:03:17,248 --> 00:03:20,000
<i>So I decided to go home
during my lunch break.</i>

47
00:03:21,151 --> 00:03:23,404
- <i>My wife wasn't home.</i>
- Azusa?

48
00:03:23,404 --> 00:03:25,280
<i>Since our son was at daycare,</i>

49
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:29,676
<i>I figured she'd just gone out alone,
and I didn't think much of it.</i>

50
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:34,665
<i>But later I thought about it.</i>

51
00:03:34,665 --> 00:03:39,602
<i>Even though it was a clear day,
the laundry wasn't hung out to dry.</i>

52
00:03:41,338 --> 00:03:45,926
<i>I thought I'd have lunch somewhere
and head back.</i>

53
00:03:45,926 --> 00:03:48,680
<i>Then I happened to pass by here.</i>

54
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,389
Here?

55
00:03:50,389 --> 00:03:52,991
Yes, this laundromat.

56
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,997
So your wife was here...

57
00:04:00,399 --> 00:04:03,168
Yes, she was.

58
00:04:05,821 --> 00:04:09,424
<i>With your husband, the two of them.</i>

59
00:04:13,036 --> 00:04:14,429
And then?

60
00:04:15,747 --> 00:04:18,083
They were talking in a friendly way.

61
00:04:18,083 --> 00:04:21,580
Relaxed, laughing gently.

62
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:24,599
I could tell by intuition
that it wasn't their first meeting.

63
00:04:26,258 --> 00:04:32,530
They finished drying their laundry
around the same time, gathered it up,

64
00:04:33,432 --> 00:04:35,533
and then walked home together.

65
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:42,415
Your husband went back to your place,
and my wife went back to our home.

66
00:04:45,728 --> 00:04:46,752
Huh?

67
00:04:48,512 --> 00:04:49,823
That's it?

68
00:04:49,823 --> 00:04:51,325
Yes.

69
00:04:51,325 --> 00:04:55,078
Like, did they go to
either person's house after that?

70
00:04:55,078 --> 00:04:57,222
Or to that sort of...

71
00:04:58,415 --> 00:05:00,876
A love hotel? No,
they didn't go anywhere like that.

72
00:05:00,876 --> 00:05:03,587
Each went back to their own home.

73
00:05:03,587 --> 00:05:05,380
And it was broad daylight.

74
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,299
But it doesn't really matter
that it was the daytime, right?

75
00:05:07,299 --> 00:05:11,361
I mean, there are popular dramas
about things like that, aren't there?

76
00:05:12,679 --> 00:05:15,516
No, no, no, that's not it.

77
00:05:15,516 --> 00:05:18,496
Because you sounded so sure, Mr. Sonoda.

78
00:05:18,496 --> 00:05:21,730
- So I was just a bit tense.
- But this is what they said as they parted.

79
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:24,816
Well then, see you next month.

80
00:05:24,816 --> 00:05:26,709
On the third Friday.

81
00:05:35,077 --> 00:05:37,079
The third Friday...

82
00:05:37,079 --> 00:05:42,934
So the next month, June, I took a day off
on the third Friday of the month.

83
00:05:45,170 --> 00:05:47,313
<i>Without telling my wife.</i>

84
00:05:50,384 --> 00:05:52,902
Huh? Why are you pulling away from me?

85
00:05:54,513 --> 00:05:56,156
Huh? And then?

86
00:05:57,432 --> 00:06:01,920
In June, on the third Friday of the month,
did the two of them meet again?

87
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:06,233
Yes. They met at this laundromat
the same way as before,

88
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:08,877
talked, and went home together.

89
00:06:10,612 --> 00:06:13,381
- That's it?
- That's it.

90
00:06:17,824 --> 00:06:20,638
Which part of that is an affair?

91
00:06:21,832 --> 00:06:25,852
Are you the type to make a fuss about cheating
just because they made eye contact?

92
00:06:26,461 --> 00:06:29,248
Were you a middle schooler who believed
that kissing makes you pregnant?

93
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,544
Geez.

94
00:06:32,544 --> 00:06:34,970
Is there anything unusual for you
about the third Friday of the month?

95
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:38,390
Well, if I had to say,
I suppose it's a busy day at work for me.

96
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:41,600
Well... I edit a monthly magazine,
so it's the press deadline day.

97
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,712
Ah, I see. So on that day,
you're busy with work...

98
00:06:43,712 --> 00:06:46,815
So you really don't need to
force a connection.

99
00:06:46,815 --> 00:06:48,865
They were probably just friends

100
00:06:48,865 --> 00:06:51,044
- who chatted once a month.
- Friends?

101
00:06:58,035 --> 00:06:59,594
It's done.

102
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:12,288
[Episode 2]

103
00:07:18,013 --> 00:07:20,114
What filter was it again?

104
00:07:21,058 --> 00:07:23,685
The 'loved one filter'?

105
00:07:23,685 --> 00:07:26,688
But I told you, enough with that.

106
00:07:26,688 --> 00:07:32,520
- Well... I have to clean the dryer...
- It's the lint filter. Well...

107
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:35,681
There's a place
in this location that pops open.

108
00:07:36,865 --> 00:07:38,560
Is there?

109
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:41,413
I think so, but I'm not sure.

110
00:07:56,885 --> 00:07:59,070
Is this it?

111
00:08:13,443 --> 00:08:16,713
[Junko Nakabayashi]

112
00:08:34,798 --> 00:08:38,026
[Junko Nakabayashi - Answering Machine]

113
00:08:41,513 --> 00:08:45,325
<i>Sakiko? It's your mother.</i>

114
00:08:45,976 --> 00:08:47,561
<i>Are you okay?</i>

115
00:08:47,561 --> 00:08:51,273
<i>Are you eating? Are you sleeping?</i>

116
00:08:51,273 --> 00:08:54,735
<i>I'm so worried about you, Sakiko.</i>

117
00:08:54,735 --> 00:08:57,821
<i>I can't eat or sleep.</i>

118
00:08:57,821 --> 00:08:59,360
Why?

119
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,450
<i>You'll be fine, Sakiko.</i>

120
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:04,120
<i>There are plenty of
other good people out there.</i>

121
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:06,788
<i>I guarantee it.</i>

122
00:09:06,788 --> 00:09:10,542
<i>Forget about Mitsuru.</i>

123
00:09:10,542 --> 00:09:11,960
<i>It was a tragic accident.</i>

124
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:15,521
<i>Just a twist of fate.
It can't be helped, right?</i>

125
00:09:16,173 --> 00:09:19,217
<i>If you come back home,</i>

126
00:09:19,217 --> 00:09:23,820
<i>I'd be happy, and your father would surely...</i>

127
00:10:15,732 --> 00:10:18,400
- Sho, did you pack your change of clothes?
- Yeah, I did.

128
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,778
All right.

129
00:10:19,778 --> 00:10:22,906
Oh wait, your water bottle,
your water bottle... here.

130
00:10:22,906 --> 00:10:24,384
Here, your water bottle.

131
00:10:24,384 --> 00:10:26,535
- You didn't forget anything, right? Good.
- Yeah.

132
00:10:26,535 --> 00:10:28,119
Now, say "I'm off" to Mom.

133
00:10:28,119 --> 00:10:29,830
Okay.

134
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:33,474
- Okay, I'm off.
- I'm off.

135
00:10:34,125 --> 00:10:36,992
All right, let's go. Hurry, hurry.

136
00:10:36,992 --> 00:10:40,500
- Dad, the car bag, the car bag.
- Huh? Oh, the car bag.

137
00:10:41,696 --> 00:10:45,528
The A/C's off, and I've got my phone.

138
00:10:46,304 --> 00:10:47,905
Oh, the keys.

139
00:10:57,482 --> 00:10:59,584
No...

140
00:11:03,822 --> 00:11:06,215
I'm off.

141
00:11:18,837 --> 00:11:20,380
There you are.

142
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:22,440
So you smoke.

143
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:27,648
Did you hear that the meeting with PR
was changed to start at 5 p.m.?

144
00:11:27,648 --> 00:11:28,704
Yeah, I did.

145
00:11:29,556 --> 00:11:31,933
So you got an extension.

146
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:33,360
Huh?

147
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:36,254
You have to pick up your son
from daycare, right?

148
00:11:38,607 --> 00:11:41,693
What? Hey, I'm in Nagoya right now.

149
00:11:41,693 --> 00:11:44,279
And I have a meeting
first thing tomorrow morning.

150
00:11:44,279 --> 00:11:45,947
You want me to make a day trip
back and forth?

151
00:11:45,947 --> 00:11:48,199
Oh, right. Sorry.

152
00:11:48,199 --> 00:11:50,260
<i>Mom was worried too.</i>

153
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:52,416
- Huh?
- <i>She said that she wants to help,</i>

154
00:11:52,416 --> 00:11:54,873
<i>but she can't just go to Tokyo right away.</i>

155
00:11:54,873 --> 00:11:57,709
Oh, I didn't realize
we'd be so short-handed...

156
00:11:57,709 --> 00:11:59,628
One possibility is

157
00:11:59,628 --> 00:12:02,496
that we could have Sho
live at the house in Ibaraki.

158
00:12:02,496 --> 00:12:04,416
No, no, no. Wait, wait.

159
00:12:04,416 --> 00:12:08,140
Are you saying that I'd live apart from Sho?
Why? I don't want that.

160
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,263
Then what are you going to do from now on?

161
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:12,724
<i>Is there anyone nearby who can help?</i>

162
00:12:12,724 --> 00:12:14,575
No, I don't think so...

163
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:21,440
I hope work went well.

164
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,126
- I'm really sorry about this.
- Not at all.

165
00:12:25,487 --> 00:12:27,780
- Was everything okay?
- Oh, yes.

166
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:31,242
The daycare teacher said that
she had contacted you.

167
00:12:31,242 --> 00:12:34,428
- I was a bit nervous. No, it's fine.
- Sorry.

168
00:12:35,372 --> 00:12:37,220
Sho's asleep.

169
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:40,260
- So please, come in.
- All right, excuse me.

170
00:12:45,548 --> 00:12:47,066
Mitsuru.

171
00:12:48,593 --> 00:12:50,069
Huh?

172
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,856
No, no, no, no, no.

173
00:12:54,683 --> 00:12:56,518
Well...

174
00:12:56,518 --> 00:12:59,840
I really wanted to carry him
all the way in like this,

175
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:03,149
but I just don't know where or how
to hold a sleeping five-year-old.

176
00:13:03,149 --> 00:13:05,151
So...

177
00:13:05,151 --> 00:13:08,170
- Please, go ahead.
- Sorry to intrude.

178
00:13:10,991 --> 00:13:12,425
Sorry.

179
00:13:14,285 --> 00:13:15,720
Well...

180
00:13:17,038 --> 00:13:19,515
What about asking family to help?

181
00:13:22,001 --> 00:13:25,755
My parents' place is in Ibaraki,

182
00:13:25,755 --> 00:13:32,637
and my father is in poor health,
so my mother is taking care of him.

183
00:13:32,637 --> 00:13:36,020
And my sister started a business in Nagoya.

184
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:39,424
So I really can't ask them for more help.
I'm really sorry.

185
00:13:39,424 --> 00:13:40,911
No, no, don't worry about it.

186
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,815
What about your wife's family?

187
00:13:43,815 --> 00:13:47,060
My wife didn't have any parents originally.

188
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,194
Originally?

189
00:13:48,832 --> 00:13:51,156
Well, I suppose nobody is born
without parents, but, well...

190
00:13:51,156 --> 00:13:53,174
She grew up in an institution.

191
00:13:55,034 --> 00:13:56,870
My husband is the same way.

192
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,371
Oh, really?

193
00:13:58,371 --> 00:14:00,980
I hear that it wasn't an institution, though.

194
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:05,130
Both his parents and relatives are estranged
from him, and I've never met them either.

195
00:14:06,528 --> 00:14:12,218
I'm not sure if his parents
even know that he's missing.

196
00:14:12,218 --> 00:14:13,861
I see.

197
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:17,472
Would you like something to drink?

198
00:14:17,472 --> 00:14:19,867
Because they had
similar backgrounds like that,

199
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:23,996
they hit it off,

200
00:14:25,273 --> 00:14:28,709
and were drawn to each other
to fill a sense of loss.

201
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,360
Right?

202
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,824
Even if you said "Right?",

203
00:14:34,824 --> 00:14:38,624
we concluded that they just chatted
at the laundromat, and that's it.

204
00:14:38,624 --> 00:14:41,790
- But they were on the same bus.
- That was a coincidence.

205
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:44,141
They were sitting next to each other.

206
00:14:46,961 --> 00:14:49,255
Even though there were other empty seats.

207
00:14:49,255 --> 00:14:50,715
What?

208
00:14:50,715 --> 00:14:53,317
<i>- We're heading to Nagano.
- Look, here it is.</i>

209
00:14:54,219 --> 00:14:58,200
<i>- Yay! Looking forward to Nagano.
- Nagano!</i>

210
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:03,494
The bereaved family gave me this video,
saying it was probably their last moments.

211
00:15:05,563 --> 00:15:07,873
Their last moments being this.

212
00:15:10,401 --> 00:15:11,456
Well?

213
00:15:15,365 --> 00:15:18,843
You didn't ask your husband
who he was going with or where, right?

214
00:15:21,079 --> 00:15:24,290
If they were just friends,
he probably would have said so.

215
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:28,096
And even more so if it was a friend
of the opposite gender.

216
00:15:28,096 --> 00:15:29,216
To avoid a misunderstanding.

217
00:15:29,216 --> 00:15:31,280
- That's...
- The fact that he didn't say anything means

218
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,056
that he couldn't say.

219
00:15:35,176 --> 00:15:39,113
It means he was doing something wrong
that he couldn't talk about.

220
00:15:40,223 --> 00:15:42,058
That's...

221
00:15:42,058 --> 00:15:43,540
Right?

222
00:15:44,352 --> 00:15:46,229
"Right?"

223
00:15:46,229 --> 00:15:48,706
Please don't ask for agreement
with just a single syllable.

224
00:15:51,442 --> 00:15:54,044
Well, you don't want to believe it, do you?

225
00:15:56,781 --> 00:15:59,467
He might still be alive.

226
00:16:01,035 --> 00:16:06,207
So, Mr. Sonoda, just because
you can't confirm the facts with your wife,

227
00:16:06,207 --> 00:16:08,434
you're jumping to conclusions
based on speculation?

228
00:16:09,335 --> 00:16:11,228
That's ridiculous.

229
00:16:11,838 --> 00:16:13,564
Your tone has been, all along, like

230
00:16:14,299 --> 00:16:18,319
you almost want them
to have been having an affair.

231
00:16:21,097 --> 00:16:22,573
Ah.

232
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,688
Maybe I do.

233
00:16:26,688 --> 00:16:28,229
Please deny it.

234
00:16:28,229 --> 00:16:30,790
Maybe it's because I'd rather just hate her.

235
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:37,129
If I could hate her,
it surely wouldn't hurt this much.

236
00:16:38,698 --> 00:16:40,424
I feel the same way you do.

237
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:44,345
It's hard to believe that
my wife would have an affair.

238
00:16:45,872 --> 00:16:48,891
She was a little hard to pin down,

239
00:16:50,793 --> 00:16:55,231
but she was straightforward
and said what was on her mind,

240
00:16:57,133 --> 00:17:03,656
and she expressed her emotions pretty well,
properly getting angry or acting spoiled.

241
00:17:04,474 --> 00:17:06,992
Above all, she hated anything
that was crooked.

242
00:17:08,227 --> 00:17:11,904
Before we got married,
when we were on a train,

243
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:15,918
she saw a high schooler who wouldn't
give up his seat to an elderly person.

244
00:17:17,487 --> 00:17:19,872
She started seriously lecturing them,

245
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:24,256
and I was so embarrassed,

246
00:17:27,872 --> 00:17:30,140
but I was also proud.

247
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:37,439
That was when I decided that
I wanted to marry her.

248
00:17:41,219 --> 00:17:43,737
Sorry, what were we just talking about?

249
00:17:47,892 --> 00:17:50,436
I think the term 'affair' is well coined.

250
00:17:50,436 --> 00:17:53,163
Was that what we were talking about?

251
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:56,166
It means going against ethics.

252
00:17:57,402 --> 00:18:01,152
But, if that's the case,

253
00:18:02,016 --> 00:18:06,302
Mitsuru absolutely didn't have an affair.

254
00:18:08,079 --> 00:18:13,017
Mitsuru, and your wife, Mr. Sonoda.

255
00:18:15,503 --> 00:18:17,984
Good people don't go against ethics.

256
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,569
But...

257
00:18:25,096 --> 00:18:27,072
Let's prove it together.

258
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:31,619
When Mitsuru comes back,
I'll ask him directly.

259
00:18:32,228 --> 00:18:35,414
But until then,

260
00:18:36,107 --> 00:18:40,461
let's gather evidence on our end
and clear things up.

261
00:18:41,321 --> 00:18:44,798
But there's a possibility that the facts
might not be so clean, you know what I mean?

262
00:18:45,450 --> 00:18:47,509
We'll deal with that when the time comes.

263
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:54,892
And there's also a perk. It'll be easier
for both of us to step into new relationships.

264
00:18:56,335 --> 00:18:58,854
You sure are positive.

265
00:19:02,008 --> 00:19:06,820
Even if we have to force it,
let's try to look for a positive direction.

266
00:19:10,933 --> 00:19:12,576
Right?

267
00:19:13,394 --> 00:19:14,979
Whoa, you startled me.

268
00:19:14,979 --> 00:19:16,481
Sorry.

269
00:19:16,481 --> 00:19:18,274
Oh, no problem.

270
00:19:18,274 --> 00:19:21,520
- Anyway, sorry for the trouble.
- Not at all.

271
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:23,613
If there's anything else, let me know.

272
00:19:23,613 --> 00:19:26,048
Thank you very much.

273
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:30,719
All right Sho, let's go.

274
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,056
Okay.

275
00:19:34,957 --> 00:19:37,792
Oh, so it's okay to carry him like that.

276
00:19:37,792 --> 00:19:41,313
Yes, a five-year-old's body
is surprisingly sturdy.

277
00:19:45,568 --> 00:19:50,489
And you shouldn't say that
you "carry" a child.

278
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,768
Good point.

279
00:19:54,336 --> 00:19:56,120
I'll be careful not to say that.

280
00:19:57,271 --> 00:19:59,023
Mitsuru, an affair?

281
00:19:59,023 --> 00:20:01,020
There's no way he did that.

282
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:02,735
At least, I know he didn't,

283
00:20:02,735 --> 00:20:06,656
but someone has cast suspicion
on Mitsuru for having an affair.

284
00:20:06,656 --> 00:20:08,991
In the absence of the person in question?

285
00:20:08,991 --> 00:20:11,051
Both parties involved are absent.

286
00:20:11,911 --> 00:20:14,500
What are you hoping to accomplish
by investigating that?

287
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:17,625
We just want to clear things up
and feel better about the situation.

288
00:20:17,625 --> 00:20:20,728
You know, I'm having an affair.

289
00:20:22,296 --> 00:20:24,512
My boyfriend... He's married.

290
00:20:25,466 --> 00:20:26,775
Huh?

291
00:20:27,969 --> 00:20:29,862
You were deceived?

292
00:20:30,596 --> 00:20:32,390
But it's okay.

293
00:20:32,390 --> 00:20:35,726
His wife knows that he has a girlfriend,

294
00:20:35,726 --> 00:20:37,580
and she accepts it.

295
00:20:41,023 --> 00:20:44,110
Sorry, I don't quite get it.

296
00:20:44,110 --> 00:20:46,362
To put it simply,

297
00:20:46,362 --> 00:20:48,364
<i>Takuma Araki, 30 years old.</i>

298
00:20:48,364 --> 00:20:50,700
<i>Office worker at a foreign company.</i>

299
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,619
<i>Married five years ago
to a wife of the same age.</i>

300
00:20:53,619 --> 00:20:55,538
<i>No children.</i>

301
00:20:55,538 --> 00:20:58,791
<i>Apparently, he's always had a girlfriend
even after getting married.</i>

302
00:20:58,791 --> 00:21:00,928
<i>And his wife accepts that.</i>

303
00:21:02,462 --> 00:21:03,552
Now do you get it?

304
00:21:06,215 --> 00:21:08,692
No, I still don't really get it.

305
00:21:09,719 --> 00:21:12,472
I don't know about other people,

306
00:21:12,472 --> 00:21:16,450
but if everyone involved is okay with it,
then maybe it's fine.

307
00:21:18,186 --> 00:21:20,688
And you're okay with that, Chizuru?

308
00:21:20,688 --> 00:21:25,985
Because I'm not bothering anyone, right?
There aren't any children being sacrificed.

309
00:21:25,985 --> 00:21:29,046
So who has the right to blame me?

310
00:21:31,991 --> 00:21:33,967
Shampoo, shampoo.

311
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:37,152
Ow! What the heck?

312
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,478
[Shopping list: soap, shampoo]

313
00:21:46,506 --> 00:21:48,160
You buy it yourself?

314
00:22:18,788 --> 00:22:20,639
Sorry to keep you waiting.

315
00:22:22,816 --> 00:22:24,192
This way.

316
00:22:25,962 --> 00:22:29,590
Huh? Is Sho in daycare even on weekends?

317
00:22:29,590 --> 00:22:31,180
No.

318
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:37,890
Yesterday my mother suddenly showed up
and forcibly took him back to their place.

319
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:38,976
Huh?

320
00:22:40,142 --> 00:22:42,496
The state of my messy house...

321
00:22:44,188 --> 00:22:50,127
And Sho told her he'd wait for me
at your house while I was at work.

322
00:22:52,071 --> 00:22:57,593
He told her that he'd wait for me
at the neighbor lady's house.

323
00:22:58,452 --> 00:23:02,957
My mom got all huffy about me
relying on strangers in Tokyo,

324
00:23:02,957 --> 00:23:05,225
so she took Sho away from me.

325
00:23:06,877 --> 00:23:09,046
- Oh, dear...
- Yeah.

326
00:23:09,046 --> 00:23:11,048
Well, but...

327
00:23:11,048 --> 00:23:14,440
I plan to go and visit him on the weekends.

328
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:17,960
And in any case, I'm worried about
my father's health anyway.

329
00:23:20,891 --> 00:23:24,077
But for today at least, it's actually
just as well that Sho isn't here.

330
00:23:27,648 --> 00:23:28,736
Yes.

331
00:23:29,900 --> 00:23:33,821
It's just as well today.

332
00:23:33,821 --> 00:23:36,506
It'd be a bit much
to drag him around for this.

333
00:23:38,743 --> 00:23:42,976
Please keep your suspicions
about Mitsuru to yourself.

334
00:23:43,831 --> 00:23:45,120
Understood.

335
00:23:46,917 --> 00:23:48,320
[Hikouki]
Sorry to keep you waiting.

336
00:23:49,856 --> 00:23:51,200
Thank you.

337
00:23:52,006 --> 00:23:56,318
So you're the husband of Mr. Seo's friend?

338
00:23:57,386 --> 00:23:59,388
Well, yeah. That's right.

339
00:23:59,388 --> 00:24:00,448
Hello.

340
00:24:02,048 --> 00:24:03,168
And so?

341
00:24:04,518 --> 00:24:07,579
There are a few things
I want to ask you about Mitsuru.

342
00:24:08,439 --> 00:24:11,734
Naoto, did you ever meet Mitsuru
outside of this shop?

343
00:24:11,734 --> 00:24:13,652
Like on Fridays?

344
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:14,784
Sometimes.

345
00:24:15,529 --> 00:24:19,033
Ah, but I do remember that on one Thursday,

346
00:24:19,033 --> 00:24:21,869
I asked him if he wanted to go drinking
the next day during the daytime,

347
00:24:21,869 --> 00:24:22,944
but he said that he wasn't free that day.

348
00:24:23,954 --> 00:24:25,498
That was...

349
00:24:25,498 --> 00:24:26,976
It was the third Friday of the month.

350
00:24:28,584 --> 00:24:31,940
Huh? Why wasn't he free
on the third Friday of the month?

351
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:33,756
He said that he had a prior engagement.

352
00:24:33,756 --> 00:24:36,160
When was that?

353
00:24:36,884 --> 00:24:40,128
I think it was before the new year,
like in December.

354
00:24:40,864 --> 00:24:45,101
So it's been going on
for at least six months, then.

355
00:24:45,101 --> 00:24:46,394
What has?

356
00:24:46,394 --> 00:24:48,544
No, no, nothing. It's nothing.

357
00:24:50,815 --> 00:24:53,291
What do you two usually talk about?

358
00:24:53,901 --> 00:24:56,736
Mr. Seo always talked about you...

359
00:25:02,976 --> 00:25:04,000
Complaints?

360
00:25:04,704 --> 00:25:09,280
Grievances, pent-up frustrations,
selfish desires that he can't tell his wife?

361
00:25:10,084 --> 00:25:11,136
No way. Really?

362
00:25:12,256 --> 00:25:13,344
Well...

363
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:20,928
What kind of things specifically
did he complain about?

364
00:25:20,928 --> 00:25:22,080
Various things.

365
00:25:23,472 --> 00:25:25,344
Marriage is tough, isn't it?

366
00:25:31,939 --> 00:25:34,144
Are you investigating something
about Mr. Seo?

367
00:25:35,276 --> 00:25:37,696
No, don't worry about it.

368
00:25:41,073 --> 00:25:43,104
I'll go bring out the Financiers.

369
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,502
Dealing with that regular customer
is tough, isn't it?

370
00:25:53,502 --> 00:25:55,671
Good work.

371
00:25:55,671 --> 00:25:57,689
I'm exhausted.

372
00:25:58,424 --> 00:26:01,580
Is there anyone you don't get along with?

373
00:26:01,580 --> 00:26:02,970
Don't get along with?

374
00:26:02,970 --> 00:26:04,805
People you dislike.

375
00:26:04,805 --> 00:26:08,684
You're kind to everyone,
and never speak ill of anyone.

376
00:26:08,684 --> 00:26:10,624
I don't have anyone I dislike.

377
00:26:11,437 --> 00:26:13,105
Really?

378
00:26:13,105 --> 00:26:17,401
<i>There are only people I like
or people I don't care about.</i>

379
00:26:17,401 --> 00:26:19,778
<i>Don't you ever end up disliking someone?</i>

380
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:23,256
<i>There's a trick to not disliking people.</i>

381
00:26:25,242 --> 00:26:28,032
I distance myself
before I end up disliking them.

382
00:26:45,256 --> 00:26:47,733
- Welcome.
- Hello.

383
00:26:52,722 --> 00:26:54,698
You sure switched fast.

384
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:57,088
Well... this is Mrs. Seo.

385
00:26:58,478 --> 00:27:01,952
Her husband was in the same
bus accident, and is missing.

386
00:27:02,816 --> 00:27:04,512
- Nice to meet you.
- Oh, that.

387
00:27:05,777 --> 00:27:08,640
Hitting it off as a result of
being in similar circumstances,

388
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:12,258
and drawn to each other to fill the loss?

389
00:27:13,088 --> 00:27:15,995
- Something like that, right?
- We live near each other.

390
00:27:15,995 --> 00:27:18,135
And she's helped by watching my child for me.

391
00:27:18,135 --> 00:27:19,611
I see.

392
00:27:20,750 --> 00:27:22,643
Be careful.

393
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:28,864
Oh, right.

394
00:27:34,973 --> 00:27:40,095
This is the book that
Azusa was always reading during work.

395
00:27:40,095 --> 00:27:41,504
It's merchandise, but you can have it.

396
00:27:42,295 --> 00:27:44,315
"Thirst for Love".

397
00:27:44,315 --> 00:27:45,664
What's it about?

398
00:27:47,610 --> 00:27:49,120
An affair.

399
00:27:53,095 --> 00:27:55,577
What? What? What?

400
00:27:55,577 --> 00:27:59,539
Just because someone likes suspense
doesn't make them a criminal, right?

401
00:27:59,539 --> 00:28:01,416
Right?

402
00:28:01,416 --> 00:28:04,127
Just like not everyone
who likes horror is a ghost.

403
00:28:04,127 --> 00:28:05,378
Exactly.

404
00:28:05,378 --> 00:28:07,146
What's this all about?

405
00:28:07,839 --> 00:28:09,549
Well? And?

406
00:28:09,549 --> 00:28:16,071
Well... I don't know why
my wife was on that bus that day.

407
00:28:16,889 --> 00:28:19,642
And it seems that
Mrs. Seo's husband was with her.

408
00:28:19,642 --> 00:28:20,935
Oh, is that so?

409
00:28:20,935 --> 00:28:24,096
Did you hear Azusa say anything about it?
Like their destination?

410
00:28:25,523 --> 00:28:27,984
- Ah, that kind of thing.
- Yes.

411
00:28:27,984 --> 00:28:29,585
Right, right, right.

412
00:28:35,575 --> 00:28:39,829
I don't know,
but even if I did, I wouldn't tell you.

413
00:28:39,829 --> 00:28:40,830
Huh?

414
00:28:40,830 --> 00:28:45,472
Because it was something that
she didn't want to tell her husband, right?

415
00:28:47,879 --> 00:28:52,512
I think that privacy should be protected,
even after death. Don't you?

416
00:28:57,472 --> 00:29:01,951
[Thirst for Love]

417
00:29:05,312 --> 00:29:08,207
There's nothing I can't tell my husband.

418
00:29:09,692 --> 00:29:10,985
You two must be close.

419
00:29:10,985 --> 00:29:13,712
Whatever he asks me, I can answer anything.

420
00:29:14,530 --> 00:29:18,496
But since he doesn't ask much,
there's plenty that I haven't told him.

421
00:29:19,202 --> 00:29:20,544
I see.

422
00:29:21,412 --> 00:29:26,668
He firmly believes that
a married couple thinks alike.

423
00:29:26,668 --> 00:29:30,656
So he always asks for agreement
by just saying "Right?".

424
00:29:31,547 --> 00:29:34,016
Not even a word, just a syllable.

425
00:29:35,301 --> 00:29:38,179
Sometimes we're a little out of sync,
or have leftover thoughts,

426
00:29:38,179 --> 00:29:42,100
but I'd actually like to
enjoy hashing those things out.

427
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:44,994
But Itsuki likes things
that aren't like that.

428
00:29:47,855 --> 00:29:49,873
What's this story about?

429
00:29:50,984 --> 00:29:52,710
An affair.

430
00:29:55,195 --> 00:29:56,714
An affair.

431
00:29:59,867 --> 00:30:03,162
Sorry, that old man has no morals.

432
00:30:03,162 --> 00:30:04,847
He was quite...

433
00:30:05,615 --> 00:30:08,000
He was quite a character.

434
00:30:09,715 --> 00:30:11,520
Maybe I'm the one with no morals.

435
00:30:13,464 --> 00:30:18,315
Just because someone is dead doesn't mean
it's okay to pry into everything.

436
00:30:18,315 --> 00:30:20,722
Sorry, I'm the one who started it.

437
00:30:20,722 --> 00:30:22,948
No, no. I went along with it.

438
00:30:24,851 --> 00:30:30,912
Just because you're married doesn't mean
you have the right to know everything, right?

439
00:30:32,984 --> 00:30:34,464
Even that day,

440
00:30:35,570 --> 00:30:41,952
if the accident hadn't happened,
I'd probably still know nothing.

441
00:30:46,497 --> 00:30:48,557
And that would have been fine.

442
00:30:50,042 --> 00:30:52,061
Even if it was an affair or whatever,

443
00:30:53,296 --> 00:30:55,481
even if there was something I didn't know,

444
00:30:56,340 --> 00:30:58,848
as long as my wife came back home alive,
that would have been enough.

445
00:31:04,098 --> 00:31:05,472
Sorry.

446
00:31:07,685 --> 00:31:09,024
Mr. Sonoda.

447
00:31:10,176 --> 00:31:11,680
Are you eating properly?

448
00:31:12,857 --> 00:31:15,200
Without Sho, you'd be even more likely
to just eat whatever's easy...

449
00:31:25,870 --> 00:31:28,128
That was my mother calling. No worries.

450
00:31:31,459 --> 00:31:34,752
Well, what was I just saying?

451
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:38,784
Are you eating okay?

452
00:31:41,260 --> 00:31:43,776
I'll ask around
among my wife's acquaintances too.

453
00:31:44,384 --> 00:31:45,515
Huh?

454
00:31:45,515 --> 00:31:48,032
Your husband will surely come back.

455
00:31:51,354 --> 00:31:54,592
Let's wait for him feeling refreshed,
and with a clear mind.

456
00:31:59,695 --> 00:32:01,338
Okay.

457
00:32:36,190 --> 00:32:38,067
See you tomorrow.

458
00:32:38,067 --> 00:32:41,420
- Bye-bye.
- Goodbye.

459
00:32:42,432 --> 00:32:44,195
All right.

460
00:32:44,195 --> 00:32:45,504
Oh, hello.

461
00:32:46,336 --> 00:32:48,578
- Are you Sho's father?
- Oh, yes.

462
00:32:48,578 --> 00:32:50,454
Thank you for the other day.

463
00:32:50,454 --> 00:32:53,615
Not at all. That must have been tough.

464
00:32:53,615 --> 00:32:56,294
You were very close to my wife.

465
00:32:56,294 --> 00:32:57,495
Yes.

466
00:32:57,495 --> 00:33:00,672
So, on the day of the accident,

467
00:33:00,672 --> 00:33:03,840
did you happen to ask her
where she was planning to go?

468
00:33:04,969 --> 00:33:06,432
I didn't ask,

469
00:33:07,168 --> 00:33:09,632
but maybe it was a spontaneous solo trip?

470
00:33:10,850 --> 00:33:14,854
- She often said she liked that kind of thing.
- Right.

471
00:33:14,854 --> 00:33:20,335
Also, did she mention any complaints
she'd had about me recently?

472
00:33:20,335 --> 00:33:22,945
I mean, even if she did have any complaints,
I imagine it'd be hard to say,

473
00:33:22,945 --> 00:33:28,064
- so did she ever...
- I already miss hearing her gush about you.

474
00:33:32,205 --> 00:33:36,058
[Hikouki]

475
00:33:37,084 --> 00:33:38,368
Good evening.

476
00:33:41,505 --> 00:33:45,259
Sorry, but since I'm by myself,
I have to close the shop at eight.

477
00:33:45,259 --> 00:33:49,931
That's just as well... well...
I'm here to ask you about Seo-san.

478
00:33:49,931 --> 00:33:51,682
Didn't we already talk about him?

479
00:33:51,682 --> 00:33:55,680
I thought there might be something
you couldn't say in front of Seo-san.

480
00:33:57,438 --> 00:34:00,191
When you say "Seo-san", do you mean Sakiko?

481
00:34:00,191 --> 00:34:01,359
Yes.

482
00:34:01,359 --> 00:34:03,456
Because I call the shop manager "Seo-san".

483
00:34:05,446 --> 00:34:09,248
So the manager's wife, Sakiko, is "Seo-san".

484
00:34:10,201 --> 00:34:12,620
That's a bit confusing.

485
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:14,752
Married couples are confusing.

486
00:34:20,586 --> 00:34:23,040
- Coffee okay?
- Yes, please.

487
00:34:29,248 --> 00:34:36,227
Seo-san's husband... Mitsuru...
Did he really complain about Sakiko?

488
00:34:36,227 --> 00:34:37,792
No, I never heard him do that.

489
00:34:39,063 --> 00:34:40,768
Ah, that's what I figured.

490
00:34:42,316 --> 00:34:43,840
You're here to confirm that?

491
00:34:45,069 --> 00:34:48,512
Seo-san's just putting on a brave front.

492
00:34:48,512 --> 00:34:50,304
Her mental state
is actually pretty worn down.

493
00:34:51,492 --> 00:34:53,077
Yeah, that figures.

494
00:34:53,077 --> 00:34:54,784
We still don't know if he's alive or not.

495
00:34:56,330 --> 00:34:59,255
He was always gushing about her.

496
00:34:59,255 --> 00:35:00,960
It was always "Sakiko, Sakiko", all the time.

497
00:35:02,375 --> 00:35:04,576
And Seo-san too. Always "Mitsuru, Mitsuru".

498
00:35:06,048 --> 00:35:07,328
They were really close.

499
00:35:09,010 --> 00:35:13,472
But just because they were close
doesn't mean they couldn't have an affair.

500
00:35:14,807 --> 00:35:16,000
That's a harsh opinion.

501
00:35:18,352 --> 00:35:19,995
An affair?

502
00:35:19,995 --> 00:35:24,992
A younger, pretty woman he met
at the laundromat every third Friday, right?

503
00:35:26,902 --> 00:35:29,087
Did you hear that from Seo-san?

504
00:35:29,989 --> 00:35:32,064
Who do you think I heard it from?
Which Seo-san?

505
00:35:36,162 --> 00:35:37,888
Was it Azusa, huh?

506
00:35:39,749 --> 00:35:42,755
And the same last name, right?
What was it again?

507
00:35:46,547 --> 00:35:49,216
That's not good, is it?

508
00:35:49,216 --> 00:35:53,184
Married to such a good person,
and yet he has another woman.

509
00:35:54,305 --> 00:35:58,304
And he didn't expect
that woman would be married too.

510
00:36:02,354 --> 00:36:03,955
I see.

511
00:36:03,955 --> 00:36:07,616
I'm envious, and also resentful.

512
00:36:09,528 --> 00:36:14,272
There's a name for that feeling
where envy and resentment coexist.

513
00:36:16,494 --> 00:36:17,600
It's jealousy.

514
00:36:22,458 --> 00:36:24,755
Do you like Sakiko?

515
00:36:24,755 --> 00:36:26,048
How did you come to that conclusion?

516
00:36:26,962 --> 00:36:29,856
- I just lost my wife.
- That's exactly why.

517
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:34,336
It's perfect timing, isn't it?

518
00:36:36,013 --> 00:36:40,395
If you were cheated on,
you'd just switch right away with no guilt.

519
00:36:40,395 --> 00:36:42,816
- There's a convenient person nearby...
- Huh?

520
00:36:45,147 --> 00:36:48,128
Don't take out your complicated crush
on a married person on me!

521
00:36:50,528 --> 00:36:53,536
And don't you take out
being cheated on on me!

522
00:37:26,814 --> 00:37:28,858
- Whoa, you scared me.
- Shh!

523
00:37:28,858 --> 00:37:30,144
Sho finally fell asleep!

524
00:37:31,296 --> 00:37:34,304
- Okay, okay.
- Hey, hey.

525
00:37:34,304 --> 00:37:36,824
- Wait... huh? Seriously?
- Yep.

526
00:37:36,824 --> 00:37:38,240
No, wait... seriously?

527
00:37:38,912 --> 00:37:42,112
This T-shirt...
It shrank a little in the wash.

528
00:37:42,112 --> 00:37:45,249
- I bought them just my size, you know.
- Okay, okay, sorry.

529
00:37:45,249 --> 00:37:46,816
Hey, wait, wait.

530
00:37:46,816 --> 00:37:47,949
What?

531
00:37:47,949 --> 00:37:49,879
There aren't any.

532
00:37:49,879 --> 00:37:52,055
I'm going to the convenience store.

533
00:37:52,055 --> 00:37:54,383
Come on, it's fine. We're a married couple.

534
00:37:54,383 --> 00:37:56,096
Hang on. Wait, wait.

535
00:37:56,096 --> 00:37:59,808
If we're going to have a second child,
this time next year would be perfect.

536
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:05,394
If you get pregnant now,

537
00:38:05,394 --> 00:38:07,771
there'd be a three-year gap with Sho, right?

538
00:38:07,771 --> 00:38:11,104
It'd be tough with school entry
and graduation overlapping.

539
00:38:13,569 --> 00:38:17,775
Well, if you can get pregnant
around this time next year,

540
00:38:17,775 --> 00:38:19,008
it'd be a four-year gap with Sho,

541
00:38:19,008 --> 00:38:21,921
plus not an early birth date,
which would be just right.

542
00:38:22,703 --> 00:38:23,744
Right?

543
00:38:24,788 --> 00:38:27,584
You really love things
that are just right, don't you, Itsuki?

544
00:38:28,209 --> 00:38:30,464
You really love things that are just perfect.

545
00:38:36,133 --> 00:38:37,536
No!

546
00:38:44,266 --> 00:38:46,201
Mr. Sonoda.

547
00:38:46,852 --> 00:38:47,968
Your timing is perfect.

548
00:38:50,147 --> 00:38:51,357
Please help me.

549
00:38:51,357 --> 00:38:53,166
Huh? What's up?

550
00:39:00,616 --> 00:39:03,343
I managed to release it
back into nature alive.

551
00:39:04,912 --> 00:39:07,331
Thank you.

552
00:39:07,331 --> 00:39:10,834
Is your husband usually
the one in charge of insect removal?

553
00:39:10,834 --> 00:39:11,935
Yes.

554
00:39:11,935 --> 00:39:16,257
I'm in charge of shrieking
and running away in panic.

555
00:39:16,257 --> 00:39:18,240
- Is that so?
- Yes.

556
00:39:19,134 --> 00:39:23,456
And lately, I've been yelling
even when there aren't any bugs.

557
00:39:24,598 --> 00:39:28,034
It seems I want to use my voice
when there's no one to talk to.

558
00:39:29,436 --> 00:39:32,256
But without a reply,
it just feels even emptier, doesn't it?

559
00:39:33,255 --> 00:39:35,025
Do you have experience with that?

560
00:39:35,025 --> 00:39:37,675
I'm living alone
for the first time in a while.

561
00:39:37,675 --> 00:39:40,135
By the way, what should I do with this?
Throw it away?

562
00:39:40,135 --> 00:39:41,944
Yes, here.

563
00:39:49,248 --> 00:39:51,333
Cigarettes.

564
00:39:51,333 --> 00:39:53,377
Yes, I smoke.

565
00:39:53,377 --> 00:39:56,521
- Sorry. It smells, doesn't it?
- No.

566
00:39:57,915 --> 00:40:00,968
I didn't notice at first,

567
00:40:00,968 --> 00:40:05,335
but when you came to pick up Sho
and stepped inside, I caught the scent.

568
00:40:05,335 --> 00:40:07,433
And since then, occasionally...

569
00:40:07,433 --> 00:40:10,561
Yes, on that day.

570
00:40:10,561 --> 00:40:13,824
I just happened to pick it up again
after a long time.

571
00:40:13,824 --> 00:40:16,096
I quit it after having a child.

572
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:25,536
I knew it.

573
00:40:26,775 --> 00:40:28,386
Sorry.

574
00:40:30,873 --> 00:40:32,256
The same as Mitsuru's.

575
00:40:33,626 --> 00:40:36,224
Probably the same brand.

576
00:40:39,673 --> 00:40:43,744
The unlit cigarettes and the smoky smell.

577
00:40:45,095 --> 00:40:46,821
It's a little...

578
00:40:49,183 --> 00:40:50,944
different from Mitsuru's.

579
00:40:52,936 --> 00:40:58,464
It's the scent that clings to a smoker's clothes
after a little time has passed.

580
00:41:08,243 --> 00:41:10,752
I finally found this scent.

581
00:41:39,942 --> 00:41:41,568
I'm sorry.

582
00:41:46,073 --> 00:41:48,672
Your height is just about the same too.

583
00:41:52,413 --> 00:41:53,504
That's why.

584
00:41:57,084 --> 00:41:58,496
Sorry.

585
00:42:01,935 --> 00:42:03,424
I knew it.

586
00:42:05,551 --> 00:42:07,872
What shampoo do you use?

587
00:42:09,805 --> 00:42:11,232
It's the same scent.

588
00:42:15,144 --> 00:42:19,520
Do you not know which refill to buy?

589
00:42:20,816 --> 00:42:22,560
I'm having trouble with it.

590
00:42:25,571 --> 00:42:27,520
I bought various ones,
but they're all different.

591
00:42:29,199 --> 00:42:30,528
My hair gets squeaky.

592
00:42:33,620 --> 00:42:35,616
I have some stocked here at home.

593
00:42:36,790 --> 00:42:38,784
I can give you that for now.

594
00:42:40,586 --> 00:42:41,856
Thank you.

595
00:42:50,888 --> 00:42:54,496
Please wait here just a moment.

596
00:42:56,685 --> 00:43:01,024
I'll go get the refill in just a bit.

597
00:43:24,555 --> 00:43:26,400
You have a phone call.

598
00:43:27,616 --> 00:43:29,312
I have a bad feeling about this.

599
00:43:38,727 --> 00:43:42,622
[Nagano Prefectural Police]

600
00:43:49,376 --> 00:43:50,464
[This drama is fiction]

601
00:43:50,464 --> 00:43:51,552
[Any organizations, names, or persons
appearing are unrelated to actual entities]

602
00:43:51,552 --> 00:43:52,640
[Smoking scenes are filmed with consideration
for the health of the cast and crew]

603
00:43:52,640 --> 00:43:55,808
I'd probably still know nothing.

604
00:43:55,808 --> 00:43:58,592
There's nothing I can't tell my husband.

605
00:43:58,592 --> 00:44:01,472
And don't you take out
being cheated on on me!

606
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:04,192
I distance myself
before I end up disliking them.
